  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> mole of ideal gas is allowed to expand reversibly and adiabatically from a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The work done is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The final temperature of the gas is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> (Nearest integer). Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From first law of thermodynamics:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math><br />We know for adiabatic process,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>150</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>",
